WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Care Gap Explorer is a portfolio healthcare data application

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.190
built around a synthetic diabetes cohort.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.055
The Home page provides an operational view of the population

00:00:11.095 --> 00:00:14.780
and highlights patients with open A1C monitoring gaps.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.530
Care Gaps turns those results into a work queue.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.760
Users can distinguish patients who are overdue

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.670
from patients with no recorded A1C.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.320
Opening a patient provides the evidence behind the status,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.910
including A1C history, encounters, medications and procedures.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.533
Tasks adds a demonstration workflow layer for tracking review and follow-up

00:00:39.573 --> 00:00:43.180
without changing the underlying clinical gap status.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.430
Analytics moves back to the population level to examine monitoring coverage,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:53.690
gap composition, testing over time, age groups and care settings.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:58.650
Ask AI provides a conversational way to explore the synthetic cohort,

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:04.040
including follow-up questions, calculation explanations and SQL when requested.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.790
Throughout the application, clinical source data, derived measures

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:11.640
and demonstration workflow data are kept separate.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.914
The result is an end-to-end example of transforming healthcare data

00:01:15.954 --> 00:01:19.480
into a measurable and explainable care-gap workflow.
